---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="The Blueprint" description="A repeatable methodology for strategic clarity.">
  <section class="container section grid gap-8">
    <div class="reveal flex flex-col gap-4">
      <span class="kicker">The Methodology</span>
      <h1 class="serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl">A repeatable way to make the right calls.</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[color:var(--muted)] max-w-2xl">
        This is the process I use to turn technical detail into a story people trust, and to help
        teams build products that are ready for the next stage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <div class="reveal p-6 rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--line)] bg-[color:var(--bg-elev)]">
        <span class="tag">01</span>
        <h2 class="serif text-2xl mt-4">The Translation Layer</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[color:var(--muted)]">
          Turn engineering specs into customer confidence. Simple words, clear flow, fewer surprises.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal p-6 rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--line)] bg-[color:var(--bg-elev)]">
        <span class="tag">02</span>
        <h2 class="serif text-2xl mt-4">The Exit Framework</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[color:var(--muted)]">
          Position the product for acquisition with clean positioning, clear metrics, and proof of demand.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-[color:var(--muted)]">
          Examples: Props to Realtor.com. Nudge to WEST.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal p-6 rounded-2xl border border-[color:var(--line)] bg-[color:var(--bg-elev)]">
        <span class="tag">03</span>
        <h2 class="serif text-2xl mt-4">The Community Flywheel</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[color:var(--muted)]">
          Use advisory boards and peer networks to pressure-test the roadmap before launch.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
